Optimization System level coordination

274
00:18:49,009 --> 00:18:53,380
can produce goal directed behavior without
requiring individual components

275
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:58,099
to be goal directed themselves. Emergent
goal directedness arises

276
00:18:58,099 --> 00:19:02,539
when multiple components, whether separate
AI systems, external tools,

277
00:19:02,539 --> 00:19:07,259
or architectural elements, interact in
ways that systematically pursue

278
00:19:07,259 --> 00:19:10,619
objectives at the system level, even when
no single

279
00:19:10,619 --> 00:19:14,940
component implements goal pursuit. Example
A simple group walking

280
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:18,690
to a restaurant exhibits emergent goal
directedness. The group

281
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:22,210
as a whole systematically moves toward the
restaurant, adapts

282
00:19:22,210 --> 00:19:26,009
to obstacles, and maintains its objective
despite individual members

283
00:19:26,170 --> 00:19:30,329
getting distracted or taking different
paths. No single person

284
00:19:30,410 --> 00:19:33,009
needs to be in charge of the goal. The

285
00:19:33,009 --> 00:19:36,690
group level behavior emerges from
individual interactions and social

286
00:19:36,690 --> 00:19:41,250
coordination. If you temporarily distract
one walker, the rest

287
00:19:41,250 --> 00:19:44,569
continue toward the restaurant and the
distracted member rejoins.

288
00:19:45,230 --> 00:19:48,190
The roles of leader and follower shift
dynamically between

289
00:19:48,190 --> 00:19:51,869
different people, yet the overall goal
pursuit remains robust.
